// - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -
// Filename:	TS044 VSC90 UV LED Driver PCB.test
// Project:		VSC90
// Author:      Foster & Freeman Ltd - Paul Evans
// Modified:    17-07-24
//
// Description: This script tests the Driver with a constant resistance using 
//              the TENMA Programmable Load and TENMA Programmable PSU. The 
//              process involves equipment setup, configuration, and 
//              evaluation of the PCB under test. The test script includes 
//              step-by-step instructions and checks for ensuring proper 
//              connection and operation of the equipment, as well as handling 
//              pass/fail conditions.
// 
// - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -

[0] force FAIL by default to avoid IMPORTANT message below.
#1: Enter operator initials and PCB serial number:
a. Enter operator intials.
b. Enter serial number into the box below.
c. Connect the PC (via USB) to the TENMA Programmable PSU.
d. Connect the PC (via USB) to the TENMA Programmable Load.
IMPORTANT: Observe ESD precautions for handling ESD sensitive devices.  
DISPLAY: 1UVDRIVERsetup.png
COMMENT: *Example image below*
CLICK_OK:

#2: Equipment Setup 1
a. Connect the VSC90 Loopback(TE210) to J3.
b. Connect the PSU lead(TE205) to the UUT at the connector J1. 
c. Connect the PSU lead(TE205) Red male banana plug to the + of CH1 on the TENMA Programmable PSU. 
d. Connect the PSU lead(TE205) Yellow male banana plug to the  +  of CH2 on the TENMA Programmable PSU.  
e. Connect the PSU lead(TE205) Black male banana plugs to the  -  of CH1 & CH2 on the TENMA Programmable PSU.
DISPLAY: TE205 Setup.jpg
COMMENT: *Example image below*
CLICK_OK:


#3: Equipment Setup 2
a. Connect the Load lead(TE206) to the UUT at the connector J2.
b. Connect the 255mnm lead of the Load lead(TE206) to the TENMA Programmable LOAD.
c. Set the PSU lead(TE205) switch to position A (255nm).
d. Set the TENMA Programmable Load output to on.
e. Set the TENMA Programmable PSU power switch to on.
DISPLAY: TE206 Setup 1.jpg
COMMENT: *Example image below*
CLICK_OK:
CONNECT: TENMAPSU
IF_NOT:
GOTO: #3: 

#4: Configure the PSU
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUT0
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OCP1
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OCPSET1:500
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OCP2
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OCPSET2:500
COMMAND: TENMAPSU VSET1:12.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU ISET1:2.500
COMMAND: TENMAPSU VSET2:12.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU ISET2:2.000


#4.1: Connect and Configure the TENMA Programmable Load.
CONNECT: TENMALOAD
IF_NOT:
GOTO: #4.1:
COMMAND: TENMALOAD :INPut OFF
COMMAND: TENMALOAD :FUNC RES
COMMAND: TENMALOAD :RESistance 62OHM
//COMMAND: TENMALOAD :RESistance 108OHM
COMMAND: TENMALOAD :INPut ON

#5:  Checking State is output OFF.	//Checking there is no current draw - if  is then the 
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUTCH1:1
DELAY: 1000
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned voltage is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0 0 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
IF:
GOTO: #6: 
IMPORTANT: This test has failed, check the ??		
PASS_FAIL: #4.1

#6: (255nm) Read the current from the TEMMA and evaluate for PASS or FAIL.
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUTCH2:1
DELAY: 2000 
COMMAND: TENMALOAD :MEAS:CURR?
READLINE: TENMALOAD TEMMAcurrent
The returned voltage is =  %TEMMAcurrent%
RANGE: %TEMMAcurrent% 0.240 0.05 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 						
SUB: TestPassOrFail

#7: Check system for is in off state before start.
COMMAND: TENMALOAD :INPut OFF
COMMAND: TENMALOAD :RESistance 62OHM
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUTCH2:0
COMMAND: TENMAPSU IOUT1?
READLINE: TENMAPSU PSUcurrent
The returned voltage is =  %PSUcurrent%
RANGE: %PSUcurrent% 0.0 0.0 // set the range as per TS014_TEST_SEQUENCER_scripts.docx 
SUB: TestPassOrFail

#8: Set the PSU lead(TE205) switch to position B (308nm).
a. Set the PSU lead(TE205) switch to position B (308nm).
b. Disconnect the 255mnm lead of the Load lead(TE206) from the TENMA Programmable LOAD.
c. Connect the 308mnm lead of the Load lead(TE206) to the TENMA Programmable LOAD.
IMPORTANT: Set the UV PSU lead(TE205) switch to position B (308nm)
DISPLAY: Test8Setup.jpg
COMMENT: *Example image below*
CLICK_OK:


#9: (308nm) Read the current from the TEMMA and evaluate for PASS or FAIL.
IMPORTANT: Set the UV PSU lead(TE205) switch to position B (308nm)
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUTCH2:1
COMMAND: TENMALOAD :INPut ON
DELAY: 1000
COMMAND: TENMALOAD :MEAS:CURR?
READLINE: TENMALOAD TEMMAcurrent
The returned voltage is =  %TEMMAcurrent%
RANGE: %TEMMAcurrent% 0.327 0.05						
SUB: TestPassOrFail


#10: Turning off the load.
COMMAND: TENMALOAD :INPut OFF
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUT0


#11: Test complete.
COMMAND: TENMALOAD :INPut OFF
IF: %FAILED% > 0
GOTO: #Failed:
ELSE: #Passed:


#Failed: A test failed
This PCB has failed to pass all Tests
Check the Log file for more details on the failed test(s).
IMPORTANT: This PCB has failed to pass all Tests
DISPLAY: test_failed.png
CLICK_OK:
GOTO: #QUIT:

#Passed: next test
a. All tests instructions have been completed and a log file created.
b. Click OK to finish and power OFF.
DISPLAY: AllTestsPassed.png
CLICK_OK:

#QUIT:
COMMAND: TENMALOAD :INPut OFF
COMMAND: TENMAPSU VSET1:0.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU ISET1:0.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU VSET2:0.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU ISET2:0.00
COMMAND: TENMAPSU OUT0
DISCONNECT: TENMALOAD
DISCONNECT: TENMAPSU 
// End of file
// - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -